# The annotations of the loader's last two pieces, tape blocks 37 ($BE5D-$BECF) and 39 ($BF21-$BF2F): the source of
# src/loader/final.asm and timeend.asm (../../kit/mkgame.py --part src/loader/final-be5d.json and final-bf21.json,
# each part's image takes the module inside it). Format: ../../../../docs/ann-format.md. Witness: c1
# (work/stage1/rec/c1), the bootstrap entered at frame 23974; the blocks decoded by tools/mktape.py --decode.

@equ $5B00 Bank5Code 9472 ; the game's $5B00-$7FFF, loaded XORed with $AD
@equ $8000 Bootstrap ; the bootstrap (src/game), the last block of the tape
@equ $BED0 TimeFailed ; non-zero when the timing check failed

@module final ; The loader's end: un-XOR the bank-5 block, jump to the bootstrap
@about Block 37 lands over TimeCheck at $BE5D, block 39 over the end of the stage at $BF21, so the stage runs into TimeEnd when the table is done.

$BE5D c Unxor5B00 ; XOR the 9472 bytes of $5B00-$7FFF with $AD, then JP Bootstrap
> The tape's block 23 holds the game's $5B00-$7FFF XORed with $AD on top of the loader's cipher: this loop takes it off. c1: the bank-5 bytes change in frames 23962-23969 (memory_at every quarter frame), the game is entered at frame 23974.

$BE70 b FinalLeftover ; Bytes no code runs: a test of TimeFailed, a wipe and a copy of the bootstrap
> Never executed in c1. They look like an earlier version of TimeEnd and of the bootstrap at $8000 (the same LDIR of $3CFF bytes from bank 1 and JP $68F4); kept as bytes of the block.

@module timeend ; The stage's new end at $BF21
@about Tape block 39 lands here, over the stage's own end; the stage runs into it when the table is done.

$BF21 c TimeEnd ; The stage's end: if TimeFailed, wipe the memory below $C3EE; else Unxor5B00
> c1: L1 1, TimeFailed zero, so JP Unxor5B00.
$BF2B TimeWipe ; DEC HL / LD (HL),0 for ever
